I built the sprint board in plain TypeScript and DOM under `src/` (`main.ts`, `board.ts`, `archive.ts`, `dom.ts`), with `src/api.js` and `src/flights.js` untouched. `./check` passes and all 26 visible tests pass, after a favicon tweak that cleared the console 404. I used 4 of the 15 runs. I was unsure about a few choices the brief leaves open: move, add and item buttons are disabled while their target column or checklist is still loading, the rename input keeps its text after a successful rename, and the board re-renders on each change so keyboard focus can be lost.